      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "CONTEXT",
          "content": "Reslizumab is a humanised anti-interleukin 5 monoclonal antibody that disrupts eosinophil maturation and promotes programmed cell death."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "We carried out a systematic review and meta-analysis to assess the efficacy and safety of the drug in patients with inadequately controlled, eosinophilic asthma."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DATA SOURCES",
          "content": "The search included the following databases: MEDLINE, EMBASE, and the Cochrane Controlled Trials Register."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "STUDY SELECTION",
          "content": "A literature review was performed to identify all published randomized double-blind, placebo-controlled trials of reslizumab for the treatment of inadequately controlled, eosinophilic asthma."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DATA EXTRACTION",
          "content": "Two reviewers independently extracted and verified pre-defined data fields."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Four publications including 5 RCTs that compared reslizumab with placebo. For the comparison of reslizumab with placebo, asthma exacerbation (odds ratio (OR) = 0.46, 95% confidence interval (CI) = 0.35 to 0.59, p <0.00001); a forced expiratory volume in 1 s (FEV1) (the standardized mean difference (SMD) = 0.16, 95%CI = 0.10 to 0.23, p <0.00001); Asthma Control Questionnaire (ACQ) score (the SMD = -0.26, 95%CI= -0.36 to -0.16, p <0.00001); blood eosinophil counts (the SMD = -475.62, 95%CI = -528.41 to -422.83, p <0.00001). Safety assessments included the proportion of individuals who withdrawn due to adverse event (AE) (OR = 0.60 95%CI = 0.38 to 1.17, p = 0.16) indicated that reslizumab was well tolerated."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "LIMITATIONS",
          "content": "The article didn't research the safety, efficacy of reslizumab with longer term."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "This meta-analysis indicates that reslizumab to be an effective and safe treatment for inadequately controlled, eosinophilic asthma."
        }
      ]},
